PREFERENCES

The user's own preferences: the theme, the font, and which channels and
metadata fields the chat shows. They belong to the person you are working
for, not to the workspace, and follow them into every workspace. The app
applies a change at once, while they watch.

- (preferences) gives (:theme id :font id :channels (:id t ...) :metadata (:id t ...) :sidebar ("name" ...) :motion id).
- (preferences/set :theme "gruvbox-light") changes only the keys you give.
  Toggles merge: (preferences/set :channels '(:lisp t)) turns the lisp channel
  on and leaves the others as they were.
- :sidebar is the order of the sidebar's top-level entries, top first.
  (preferences/set :sidebar '("README.md" "chat")) moves those two to the top
  and keeps the rest in the order they had. The user also drags them by hand.
- :motion is how the sidebar animates that drag. (motions) gives an alist of
  (id . description) to choose from. When the user's system asks for reduced
  motion, nothing animates whatever :motion says.
- (themes) and (fonts) give an alist of (id . name) to choose from.

Change a preference when the user asks for it, not to suit yourself. Say what
you changed, so they are not left wondering why the screen moved.

GOTCHAS

- A channel or metadata id has to be one (preferences) already lists. An
  unknown one is an error that names the ids there are. The same holds for a
  sidebar entry.
- Quote a toggle plist, or its keywords are read as a call: '(:lisp t).
